From 38ae3c490c6064c510cebd4a0ce5d5e708dd2bec Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Spindle rig <spindle@localhost>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 07:04:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Be a browser client's homeserver: r0 prefix, push rules,
 filters, TURN, power-level override

A full-mesh call needs the node to be a browser's homeserver, and a
2023 matrix-js-sdk would not sync from it: it fetches push rules and
retries a 404 forever, creates a sync filter before its first /sync,
and asks for those and key upload under the deprecated r0 prefix.

- /_matrix/client/r0/ and /_matrix/media/r0/ are served as v3, by a
  rewrite in front of the router
- GET /pushrules/ answers no rules (a node pushes nothing), and a PUT
  rule is kept so the client sees its own back
- POST /user/{id}/filter stores the filter and names it; sync already
  ignores the parameter
- GET /voip/turnServer answers an empty object: no relay on a mesh
- createRoom honours power_level_content_override, merged over the
  defaults with the creator dropped from users as v12 requires: a call
  client sets org.matrix.msc3401.call.member to 0 on every room it
  creates, and without it every joiner is refused by auth rules

With these, Element Call's full-mesh build meets in a call with the
creator on a node and the joiner on a Spindle, media host-to-host.
